From: Peter M. <petermm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Share coex_pti_print with libbtbb

The ESP32-C3 BLE controller's libbtbb.a defines coex_pti_print(), the same
symbol the Wi-Fi glue provides as a printf redirect. Linking both archives
fails with a multiple-definition error when Bluetooth is enabled.

Make the glue's definition weak, so libbtbb's strong definition wins when the
controller is linked while a Wi-Fi-only image still resolves the symbol from
the glue.

diff --git a/src/rtems_esp_glue.c b/src/rtems_esp_glue.c
--- a/src/rtems_esp_glue.c
+++ b/src/rtems_esp_glue.c
@@ -86,8 +86,8 @@
   return len;
 }
 
-#define RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(name, tag)                     \
-  int name(const char *format, ...)                     \
+#define RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF_ATTR(attr, name, tag)          \
+  attr int name(const char *format, ...)                \
   {                                                     \
     va_list ap;                                         \
     int len;                                            \
@@ -98,13 +98,17 @@
                                                         \
     return len;                                         \
   }
+
+#define RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(name, tag) \
+  RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF_ATTR(, name, tag)
 
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(pp_printf, "wifi.pp")
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(phy_printf, "wifi.phy")
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(net80211_printf, "wifi.net80211")
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(mesh_printf, "wifi.mesh")
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(sc_printf, "wifi.smartconfig")
-RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(coex_pti_print, "wifi.coex")
+/* libbtbb also exports this when the BLE controller is linked. */
+RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF_ATTR(__attribute__((weak)), coex_pti_print, "wifi.coex")
 RTEMS_ESP_PRINTF(coexist_printf, "wifi.coex")
 
 /*
